{
  "_readme": "Radio frequencies for Pandora's Box Mk1. NOAA weather-radio channels (REAL, verified against the NWS Boston transmitter table at weather.gov/box/nwr, 2026-11-14). Ham 2m/70cm repeaters: REAL, from RadioReference county amateur-radio tables (Barnstable, Bristol, Essex, Middlesex, Norfolk, Plymouth, Suffolk, Worcester counties, MA), cross-checked against the Boston Amateur Radio Club Boston-area repeater list (barc.org). GMRS repeaters: REAL, from RepeaterBook Massachusetts GMRS \"View All Systems\" (repeaterbook.com/gmrs/Display_SS.php?state_id=25), fetched 2026-11-19 — the full MA GMRS listing (8 rows, 7 unique after dedupe of a duplicated Plymouth entry). All repeater rows are real, sample:false. Verify on the air after arrival; repeater status can change.",
  "_source": "NOAA: NWS Boston NOAA Weather Radio transmitter table, https://www.weather.gov/box/nwr. Ham: RadioReference county amateur radio pages (radioreference.com/db/browse/ctid/<id>/ham), 8 eastern MA counties, fetched 2026-11-19; cross-checked vs BARC Boston-area list. GMRS: RepeaterBook GMRS Massachusetts, https://www.repeaterbook.com/gmrs/Display_SS.php?state_id=25, fetched 2026-11-19. Note: RepeaterBook API export now requires an auth token (401) and the query CSV export is retired (410); myGMRS requires a free account + FCC GMRS license. Data above was taken from the public web listings, not the API.",
  "_format": [
    "name",
    "kind (ham | gmrs | noaa)",
    "frequency_mhz (number)",
    "tone (CTCSS Hz, or \"\" / digital code)",
    "location",
    "note",
    "sample (true = sample data, false = verified real)"
  ],
